1
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,260
Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,900
Good morning, Mr. Moto.

3
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,580
Ah, Taya, good morning.

4
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,657
Yugi's upstairs getting ready.

5
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:13,897
I'll call him for you.

6
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:15,637
Would you like something to drink?

7
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,920
Uh, no thanks. We're already late.

8
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:19,620
Yuki, Taya's here!

9
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,286
I'll be right there, Grandpa!

10
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,417
This new chain ought to keep
my Millennium Puzzle safe.

11
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,500
Seems like everyone wants
their hands on it lately.

12
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,586
And we're going to need
it now more than ever.

13
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:32,970
We are?

14
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,940
What do you mean by that?

15
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,257
The Millennium Puzzle connects us, Yuki.

16
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,811
And I sense fate has more in store for us.

17
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:43,577
Well, we're in this
together no matter what.

18
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:44,490
Good.

19
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:48,120
I wish I knew more, but our
future is still unclear to me.

20
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,660
Well, I'll help you figure it out.

21
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,920
About time, Yugi. Sorry, Thea.

22
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,737
We're going to be late for the big game.

23
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:57,114
What took you so long?

24
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,750
I...

25
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,837
I was talking to the spirit
of the Millennium Puzzle.

26
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,297
He seems kind of worried.

27
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,210
About what?

28
00:02:03,293 --> 00:02:04,637
About the future, I think.

29
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:07,661
He said something about
our destiny being unclear.

30
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:12,177
Ever since we defeated Pegasus together,
the spirit's been talking about fate.

31
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,672
Like there's something more he has to do.

32
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,537
When you think about it, he doesn't
really know that much about himself.

33
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,914
Like where he came from, why he's here.

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,817
But I'm babbling and we're late.

35
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,500
We should go. Oh, right.

36
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,657
The soccer game.

37
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,437
We definitely don't want to miss it.

38
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,350
See you, Mr.

39
00:02:29,433 --> 00:02:30,263
Moto.

40
00:02:30,346 --> 00:02:31,176
Bye, Grandpa.

41
00:02:31,259 --> 00:02:32,089
We'll see you later.

42
00:02:32,172 --> 00:02:33,002
Enjoy yourselves, you two.

43
00:02:33,085 --> 00:02:36,424
If the game ends early, feel free
to come back and help me sweep.

44
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:41,277
So, who do you think's
gonna win? Win? Win what?

45
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,780
Earth to Yugi.

46
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:44,569
The soccer game at school?

47
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,837
Oh, I don't know. Uh...

48
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,744
You don't really care
much about sports, do you?

49
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:51,400
Future's told.

50
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,677
Fates unfold.

51
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,113
Step up, boy, and I'll reveal
the secrets of your future.

52
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:58,060
Yugi? Huh?

53
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,920
Can you really see into the future? Yes.

54
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,120
What are you doing, Yugi? Taya,

55
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:05,337
maybe this fortune
teller can help me figure

56
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:07,817
out the fate of the
spirit inside the puzzle.

57
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:11,260
Hmm, okay, but we really
don't have that much time.

58
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:17,500
Hmm, boy, in order to tell your
future, I must hold a personal item.

59
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:18,930
Really?

60
00:03:19,013 --> 00:03:21,420
Your necklace will do nicely. My what?

61
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,480
No, I'm sorry, I can't.

62
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,484
Then I can't tell your fortune.

63
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:26,690
Yeah,

64
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:29,257
but I need it in order
to properly read your

65
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:31,900
aura to see what fate
has in store for you.

66
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:34,760
You do want to know, don't you?

67
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,400
You're faked.

68
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,640
Okay, but only for a second.

69
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,940
Yugi, I don't know about this.

70
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,857
Something's coming to me.

71
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:51,280
I see that this Millennium
Item now belongs to me.

72
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,380
My Millennium Puzzle!

73
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:57,940
Come back here!

74
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,257
He's getting away.

75
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,200
What do we do?

76
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,957
I'll follow him this way.

77
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:03,817
You try to cut him off around the corner.

78
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,420
You got it, Yugi!

79
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,677
You won't get away with this, you creep!

80
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:10,054
I can't believe I handed him my puzzle!

81
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:12,970
Arrows?

82
00:04:13,053 --> 00:04:14,840
That thief wants me to follow him!

83
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,845
This must be a trap, but
what choice do I have?

84
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,135
I can't lose the spirit of the puzzle!

85
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:26,840
I won't!

86
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,764
There's no sign of that
fortune teller anywhere!

87
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:35,160
I hope Yugi's okay.

88
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,980
Hey, Taya, what's the rush?

89
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,560
Oh, Bakura.

90
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,897
Someone stole Yugi's Millennium Puzzle.

91
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:44,810
No.

92
00:04:44,893 --> 00:04:45,723
Where is Yugi?

93
00:04:45,806 --> 00:04:46,636
In the alley.

94
00:04:46,719 --> 00:04:48,640
We split up to catch the guy.

95
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:50,717
Well, then don't let me detain you.

96
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,077
Keep looking and I'll get some help.

97
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,540
Right. Thanks, Bakura.

98
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,100
No one shall have the
Millennium Puzzle but me.

99
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:59,120
I want its power.

100
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,965
and I'll track it down
with my Millennium Ring.

101
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,220
Show me the way.

102
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:13,800
Trace the item's mystical energies
and lead me to the Millennium Puzzle.

103
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:18,117
If I control all the Millennium Items,

104
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,917
I will control power
unimaginable and I will

105
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,060
make certain that nobody stands in my way.

106
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:28,610
Hmm.

107
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,300
Which way, Ring?

108
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:37,960
Yes, Yugi and his Millennium
Puzzle are very close, very close.

109
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,790
Sorry,

110
00:05:42,873 --> 00:05:47,660
Teya, but I can't have you and your sniveling
friends interfering with my destiny.

111
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,275
Where are you hiding?

112
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:56,525
Whoever that guy was, he's leading
me like a rat through a maze.

113
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,859
But why would a thief want
his victim to follow him?

114
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,740
What's he really after?

115
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,500
The last arrow.

116
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,780
My Millennium Puzzle is here.

117
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:15,393
Even though we're apart, I can sense it.

118
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:17,340
But I don't see it.

119
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,060
I know you're in here!

120
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,317
Congratulations, little Yu-Gi.

121
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,240
You found me.

122
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,140
Or should I say, I found you.

123
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:28,400
And the Millennium Puzzle.

124
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,940
Give it back to me.

125
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,457
It's not going to be that easy for you.

126
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:35,577
If you want your puzzle back,
you'll have to fight me for it.

127
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:36,778
That's right, Yugi.

128
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,760
You and I are going to duel.

129
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:43,260
And the winner gets to
keep your Millennium Idol.

130
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:45,720
A dueling arena?

131
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,837
Are you up to the challenge, Yugi?

132
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:50,260
I've been waiting for you a long time.

133
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,320
Who are you?

134
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:56,305
And what do you want with
my Millennium Puzzle?

135
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,167
I desire the power your
item contains within,

136
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:02,344
but according to the rules
of its ancient magic,

137
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,900
I have to win it from you in a duel.

138
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,840
As for who I am,

139
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:10,137
let's just say that I'm the one who shall

140
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:13,097
control your destiny as
I have controlled others,

141
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:17,004
and that I am not unfamiliar with
the power of a Millennium item.

142
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:22,427
Indeed, I understand more about their
hidden mysteries than you will ever know.

143
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,460
Take your Millennium Puzzle.

144
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,280
There are ancient
secrets buried within it,

145
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:31,027
of which you and even the spirit
that inhabits it are unaware.

146
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,760
That's why I will add it to my collection.

147
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:36,837
I won't duel you for my Millennium Puzzle.

148
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,560
It already belongs to me.

149
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,974
It's in my possession now, little Yugi.

150
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:43,780
All right, then I accept your challenge.

151
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,120
Of course you do.

152
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:49,137
If I have to duel, I'll need the
spirit of the puzzle to help me.

153
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,957
Maybe I can still connect with him.

154
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,480
I can barely hear you, Yugi.

155
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:55,520
Our bond is weak.

156
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,940
It's hard to maintain contact.

157
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:01,337
I'm afraid I won't be able
to help you with this duel.

158
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:03,244
You'll have to fight him alone.

159
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:04,490
Alone?

160
00:08:04,573 --> 00:08:06,837
But I've never fought a duel without you.

161
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:09,197
And if I'm defeated,
I'll lose you forever.

162
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,420
You can defeat him.

163
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:13,837
Just trust yourself and your
deck and you'll find the way.

164
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,750
You're right.

165
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:16,897
I've got to believe in
the heart of the cards.

166
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:18,380
Be very careful, Yugi.

167
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,377
I sense a great evil.

168
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,940
No evil spirit!

169
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:39,040
Prepare to lose your precious puzzle.

170
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,940
I don't think so.

171
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:46,440
Remember, Yugi, I have seen
your future, foretold your fate.

172
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:50,540
and this duel will be your last.

173
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,897
I don't know anything about
this duelist and now I

174
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,857
have to face him alone for
the highest stakes ever.

175
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:00,897
I don't even have the gang to back me up.

176
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:01,980
Well, here goes.

177
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,060
It's time to duel.

178
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:08,540
I place the Celtic Guardian
on the field in attack mode.

179
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,540
I've made my play, now you make yours.

180
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:14,719
I place my monster in defense mode.

181
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:18,577
What's the matter?

182
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:21,366
Don't you have the courage
to face me head-on?

183
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:23,120
I don't need to.

184
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:28,237
You're the one that better go on the
offensive if you hope to win back your puzzle.

185
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,380
All right, then.

186
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:31,440
I attack with my Celtic Guardian!

187
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,110
Huh.

188
00:09:33,193 --> 00:09:35,517
That's exactly what I
wanted you to do, Yugi.

189
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,071
Your attack is activated.

190
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:39,520
The power of my cyber jaw!

191
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,700
This machine card destroys
every monster on the field!

192
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,740
And it also requires us
to draw five new cards.

193
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:57,377
Let's see what you've got up your
pathetic sleeve this time, little Yu-Gi.

194
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:58,872
Time for a new strategy.

195
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,640
I'm placing my monster in defense mode.

196
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,797
And I'm placing mine in attack mode.

197
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:07,220
Meet Mechanical Chaser
and Ground Attacker Batra.

198
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,300
More machine cards?

199
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,420
Wait, this seems familiar.

200
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:17,036
There's only one player I know whose
deck is filled with machine cards.

201
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,580
Show yourself, Bandit Keith!

202
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,600
I was right!

203
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:28,600
But why would Bandit Keith disguise
himself and steal my Millennium Puzzle?

204
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:33,017
The last time I saw him was when he battled
Joey in the Duelist Kingdom tournament.

205
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,335
He broke the rules, but Joey beat him.

206
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:39,117
When Pegasus found out Keith was
cheating, he ejected him from the island.

207
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,553
We never saw him again.

208
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:42,780
What happened to you?

209
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:44,657
I'm not Bandit Keith.

210
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:49,220
I only speak through him since he's
become my mind-controlled slave.

211
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,270
What do you mean?

212
00:10:50,353 --> 00:10:52,220
How can this be? Tell me!

213
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:56,397
After Bandit Keith was ejected
by Pegasus from Duelist Kingdom,

214
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:59,656
he fought for his life against
the harsh ocean waters.

215
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:01,450
Help!

216
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:04,657
My followers and I were on
the way to retrieve some

217
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:07,860
very special items when we
fished him out of the sea.

218
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:11,357
I'm always looking for
new minds to control,

219
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:15,264
and Bandit Keith seemed like the
perfect puppet to do my bidding.

220
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:19,140
And, as fate would have
it, he led me right to you,

221
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:22,780
the boy who possesses the
legendary Millennium Puzzle.

222
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:26,020
Is it all sinking in now, little Yuki?

223
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,117
Now that I have found you
after all these years,

224
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:32,257
I will stop at nothing to
make your puzzle and all

225
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:35,399
of the ancient powers it
possesses within it my own.

226
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:39,057
Help me!

227
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,320
You'll never free yourself, Keith!

228
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:43,400
Let the duel continue!

229
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:46,400
I play Machine King in attack mode.

230
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:50,697
My new monster gets an extra 100 attack

231
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:53,097
points for every machine
that's on the field.

232
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:54,860
That's 300 more points!

233
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:01,500
Machine King, attack with jackpunch!

234
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:08,980
You may as well give up now.

235
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,420
It's not over yet.

236
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:13,780
I play another card in defense mode.

237
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:19,280
Your defenses are useless
against my mechanical army.

238
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:24,174
Especially now that I'm adding
this machine to my troop.

239
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:26,060
Mega Sonic!

240
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:30,997
It adds another 100 attack
points to Machine King.

241
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,020
making him even more deadly.

242
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:37,760
Machine King, attack now!

243
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,070
No!

244
00:12:42,153 --> 00:12:43,240
My stone soldier!

245
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:45,220
That's right.

246
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,160
All your defenses are gone.

247
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,830
Give up yet?

248
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,900
You have no idea of the power
you're up against, little Yugi.

249
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:56,845
No matter who this guy
is, I can't let him win.

250
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:59,097
But how can I defeat
him without the spirit?

251
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:00,010
What?

252
00:13:00,093 --> 00:13:00,923
And my friends.

253
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:03,800
Come on, guys, hurry.

254
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:05,457
Yugi may be in trouble.

255
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,011
Just point the way, Taya.

256
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,813
We're right behind you.

257
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:13,397
Yeah, any creep picks on our
buddy has to deal with us all.

258
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,310
You said it.

259
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,717
All right, people.

260
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,697
Just where do you think you're going?

261
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:20,309
You volunteered to help
at the soccer game.

262
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,694
I know, Coach, but we got an emergency.

263
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:25,208
Taya's cat has gotten sick.

264
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,077
We need to take it to the vet.

265
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,020
Please, we need to help Fluffy.

266
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:30,640
Poor Fluffy.

267
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,477
I didn't realize your
little kitty was sick.

268
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,100
Of course you can go.

269
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,310
Yes, sir.

270
00:13:37,393 --> 00:13:38,380
Thank you, Coach.

271
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,180
Save that little kitty.

272
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,957
He's really a softy at heart.

273
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:45,275
It wasn't cool to mislead Coach Morty.

274
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,230
It's an emergency.

275
00:13:46,313 --> 00:13:47,540
We had to, Taya.

276
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,360
Yeah, Yugi needs us.

277
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,860
I hope we can find him.

278
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:52,140
Come on, Yugi.

279
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:53,480
Stop stalling.

280
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,117
Unless you want to admit defeat.

281
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:57,020
I'll never give up!

282
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,660
Foolish boy.

283
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:01,120
He has no idea what he's up against.

284
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,880
His millennium puzzle is as good as mine.

285
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,197
I have too much at stake in this game.

286
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,760
So take this!

287
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,780
I play Curse of Dragons!

288
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,660
In attack mode!

289
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:18,120
And I play Gaia, the Fierce Knight!

290
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:20,160
But that's not all.

291
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:23,917
I also use my polymerization card
to combine these two monsters.

292
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:28,300
in order to create Gaia,
the Dragon Champion.

293
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:33,200
This monster can take your machines apart.

294
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:38,560
Dragon Champion, attack Mechanical
Chaser with Double Dragon Lance.

295
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,400
With Mechanical Chaser gone,

296
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:48,140
your Machine King loses 100 attack
points and you lose 750 life points.

297
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,437
Very impressive,

298
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:53,717
but what will you do when I put
my weaker monsters in defense

299
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:57,153
mode to protect them from your
Dragon Champion's attacks.

300
00:14:57,540 --> 00:15:00,480
And then play Machine Conversion Factory,

301
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:05,880
a magic card that adds 300 attack and
defense points to all of my machine cards.

302
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,340
Oh, no!

303
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:12,117
You've raised Machine
King's power even more!

304
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,277
That's right, enough to
overpower your Dragon Champion.

305
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,595
Machine King, attack!

306
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:20,840
Your offensive is over, Yugi.

307
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,412
Your champion destroyed!

308
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:26,757
I've made Keith's machine monster's
attack strength overwhelming!

309
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:30,797
So why don't you stop resisting and
just hand over your puzzle to me?

310
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:33,821
It's the inevitable
conclusion to our game anyway.

311
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,380
What am I going to do?

312
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:38,440
I have to stop him somehow! But how?

313
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:43,447
He's assembled an army of the most rare
and powerful machines in Duel Monsters!

314
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,830
Wait!

315
00:15:46,913 --> 00:15:47,743
The Summoned Skull!

316
00:15:47,826 --> 00:15:51,660
This gives me an idea, but first,
I'll have to play a magic card.

317
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:54,877
Your machines might be the
most impressive I've seen,

318
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:58,600
but they're still made out
of metal, so I play Maki-u!

319
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:02,197
You think a little mist
will destroy my machines?

320
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:06,809
It won't destroy them, but it will cause
them to rust and lower their points.

321
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:14,714
And the mist turns your machine monsters
into one gigantic lightning rod,

322
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:18,634
Which makes them the perfect
target for my Summon Skull!

323
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:24,000
Summon Skull, use your lightning
strike on Machine King now!

324
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:33,560
Any more machines for the Junk Heap?

325
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:34,837
You little...

326
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:36,420
The boy is good.

327
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:38,837
He plays much better than I had expected

328
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,137
without the spirit of
the puzzle to aid him.

329
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:44,800
but he has no idea of the
power he's up against.

330
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:49,600
My deck is full of rare monsters,
the likes of which he's never seen.

331
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,820
And when I'm through with Yu-Gi,
his Millennium Puzzle will be mine.

332
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:58,400
So, they went running
down this alley? Uh-huh.

333
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,060
Hmm, these arrows.

334
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:03,797
Hey, you think Yu-Gi tacked
these things up here for us?

335
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,957
I don't think he had the time, Joey.

336
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,860
Hey, guys, look at that!

337
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:09,417
Oh, no.

338
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:12,040
Oh, how are we gonna find him?

339
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:14,697
Now you're the one who's stalling.

340
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:16,368
Are you gonna draw or what?

341
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:21,120
I've picked the Graceful Charity card.

342
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:26,145
By placing this card on the table, I'm
able to draw three new cards from my deck.

343
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:30,037
And I'm confident that
they'll be exactly the

344
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:33,880
cards I need to end this
duel once and for all.

345
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,277
You're finished, little Yugi.

346
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:46,007
I've dropped the ultra-rare
Zero Ritual card.

347
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:50,222
It's used to summon one of the
most powerful monsters in the game.

348
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:53,810
Whoa.

349
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:56,817
I've never even heard of
the Zero Ritual card before,

350
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,997
but I've got a sneaking
suspicion that I'm about

351
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,677
to learn more about it
than I really want to know.

352
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,920
How perceptive.

353
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:07,817
For once I put Zero Ritual into
play, this duel is over. Maybe.

354
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:11,135
But activating a Ritual card
takes more than just talk.

355
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:13,917
You also need to have the right
Monster card in your hand,

356
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,765
and what are the odds of that?

357
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,040
No way!

358
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:24,225
Maybe you finally understand the
power you are up against, Yugi.

359
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,730
Now,

360
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:29,837
Sierra Ritual sacrifices
my two remaining monsters

361
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:32,637
in order to bring forth the
greatest of my creatures.

362
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:35,017
Behold the instrument of your destruction,

363
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:37,806
one of the strongest
beasts and dual monsters.

364
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:40,620
Behold, Zera the manned!

365
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:44,580
Our battle ends here!

366
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:46,797
Say goodbye to your Millennium Puzzle!

367
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,460
Zera, attack now!

368
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:58,140
Zera obliterated my Summoned
Skull, but I can't give up!

369
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:00,655
You'll never get my Millennium Puzzle!

370
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:08,580
So, my Millennium Ring has led me
here The puzzle must be inside Hmm,

371
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:12,937
I also sense a dark presence from
the Shadow Realm Seizing control

372
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:16,844
of the Millennium Puzzle might be
more interesting than I thought

373
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:19,440
Yugi, where are you?

374
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:23,200
Yugi, Yugi, say something, buddy

375
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:25,360
Where is he?

376
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:30,780
You're finished, little Yugi With
Bandit Keith under my mind control,

377
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,960
you'll never win this duel.

378
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:35,320
Help! Help!

379
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:41,080
Keith, your resistance is futile.

380
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:44,640
It's time for me to end this
duel and take what's mine.

381
00:19:44,940 --> 00:19:45,980
What do I do now?

382
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,297
I have nothing to fight this monster with.

383
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:51,077
If only I could call on the
spirit and ask for his help.

384
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,513
But we've lost contact.

385
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:55,717
I think Yugi's finally
figured out it's hopeless.

386
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:59,637
He will fall against my
superior monsters and

387
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:02,249
the Millennium puzzle
will be in my control
